[0.45, "o", "Title:      \u001b[1mShip Cloud Block Storage Normalization\u001b[0m\r\nStatus:     \u001b[1m\u001b[92mverified\u001b[39m\u001b[0m\r\nArchetype:  \u001b[95m\u001b[1mStrategic\u001b[0m\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[2m\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1mGoals\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mMG-01\u001b[0m - Convert bearing VDcStQqlo into executable board work for a canonical cloud block-storage contract across local, hosted, and SSH-owned execution lanes. (\u001b[2mVDcStQqlo\u001b[0m)\r\n  \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mMG-02\u001b[0m - Keep the mission surfaces doctor-clean and make this cloud block-storage mission visible through the board command surfaces. (\u001b[2mrun `just keel mission show VDfCa3q94`, `just flow`, and `just keel doctor`\u001b[0m)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mChildren\u001b[0m\r\n  Epics (1):\r\n    \u001b[1m\u001b[36mVDcStQqlo\u001b[39m\u001b[0m - Cloud Block Storage Normalization (\u001b[2mdone\u001b[0m)\r\n  Bearings (1):\r\n    \u001b[1m\u001b[94mVDcStQqlo\u001b[39m\u001b[0m - Cloud Block Storage Normalization (\u001b[2mlaid\u001b[0m)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mStructural Drift\u001b[0m\r\n  Coefficient: 0.63 (severe)\r\n  Coverage:    entities 302/302 | knowledge 5/43 | source 0/0 | docs 0/17\r\n  Context:     38 knowledge units lack source provenance; 17 project docs are unlinked\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mLatest Log Entry\u001b[0m\r\n    2026-03-12T07:31:36\r\n"]
[1.8, "o", "$ sed -n '1,120p' .keel/missions/VDfCa3q94/CHARTER.md\r\n"]
[2.25, "o", "# Ship Cloud Block Storage Normalization - Charter\r\n\r\n## Goals\r\n\r\n| ID | Description | Verification |\r\n|----|-------------|--------------|\r\n| MG-01 | Convert bearing VDcStQqlo into executable board work for a canonical cloud block-storage contract across local, hosted, and SSH-owned execution lanes. | board: VDcStQqlo |\r\n| MG-02 | Keep the mission surfaces doctor-clean and make this cloud block-storage mission visible through the board command surfaces. | manual: run `just keel mission show VDfCa3q94`, `just flow`, and `just keel doctor` |\r\n\r\n## Constraints\r\n\r\n- Keep the first slice bounded to storage normalization: volume identity, attachment semantics, placement or ownership language, and one proof-backed operator workflow. Do not broaden scope into a full storage service, CSI-style orchestration, k3s, or GPU work.\r\n- Use bearing VDcStQqlo plus the current artifact, rootfs, hosted-placement, and hybrid-execution artifacts as the primary sources, and preserve one canonical `port` operator surface rather than inventing a second storage-specific control plane.\r\n- Preserve the hard-cutover policy: do not add compatibility aliases, dual storage models, or fallback parsing to bridge old artifact-only semantics with the new canonical storage contract.\r\n\r\n## Halting Rules\r\n\r\n- DO NOT halt while any MG-* goal has unfinished board work\r\n- HALT when the storage-normalization work is decomposed into executable board items and only verification-oriented manual checks remain\r\n- YIELD to human when prioritization depends on provider-specific persistence guarantees, block-device API choices, or durability semantics that are not inferable from the repository\r\n"]
[3.6, "o", "$ keel epic show VDcStQqlo\r\n"]
[4.05, "o", "Title:     \u001b[1mCloud Block Storage Normalization\u001b[0m\r\nStatus:    \u001b[32mdone\u001b[39m\r\nCreated:   \u001b[2m2026-03-12 07:35:31\u001b[0m\r\nStarted:   \u001b[2m2026-03-12 07:47:30\u001b[0m\r\nUpdated:   \u001b[2m2026-03-12 08:36:19\u001b[0m\r\nCompleted: \u001b[2m2026-03-12 08:36:19\u001b[0m (\u001b[2m48m\u001b[0m)\r\nPath:      \u001b[2m/home/alex/workspace/spoke-sh/port/.keel/epics/VDcStQqlo/README.md\u001b[0m\r\nPRD:       \u001b[2m/home/alex/workspace/spoke-sh/port/.keel/epics/VDcStQqlo/PRD.md\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1mProblem\u001b[0m\r\n  Port already has a strong artifact and guest-image story, but it does not yet\r\n  publish a first-class portable block-storage contract for persistent or\r\n  ephemeral attached volumes. The current rootfs- and artifact-centric model is\r\n  credible for booting machines, but it is not enough for operator-facing\r\n  stateful workloads or for the cloud storage normalization the product horizon\r\n  now calls for.\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mGoals\u001b[0m\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m: Define one canonical storage vocabulary that separates boot artifacts from attached data volumes across local, hosted, and SSH-managed Firecracker lanes. (Planning artifacts and shared model changes keep \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mkernel\u001b[0m and \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mguest_image\u001b[0m as boot artifacts while introducing explicit attached-volume semantics. -> Epic PRD, voyage SRS/SDD, and downstream stories preserve one operator model for rootfs plus attached volumes.)\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m: Plan and ship a first executable attached-volume slice without expanding into CSI, distributed storage, or service orchestration. (One voyage scopes a bounded attached-volume lane with executable stories and proof-backed verification. -> A Firecracker-first attached-volume slice is planned and ready for operator delivery.)\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m: Make storage ownership, backend detail, and persistence semantics explicit before launch and in lifecycle surfaces. (Docs, validation, and lifecycle output tell operators which host owns a volume, which backend is in use, and whether the volume is ephemeral or persistent. -> Operators can reason about storage behavior without reading runtime code.)\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-04\u001b[0m: Preserve the existing artifact, rootfs, and machine lifecycle story for machines that do not opt into attached volumes. (Existing artifact commands and current machine launch flows continue to work without compatibility shims or silent behavior changes. -> No planned slice regresses the shipped boot-artifact workflow.)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mScope Drift\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m(no scope drift detected)\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mStructural Drift\u001b[0m\r\n  Coefficient: 0.63 (severe)\r\n  Coverage:    entities 302/302 | knowledge 5/43 | source 0/0 | docs 0/17\r\n  Context:     38 knowledge units lack source provenance; 17 project docs are unlinked\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mRequirement Coverage\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-01\u001b[39m - Port must extend the shared machine model with explicit attached-volume definitions that are distinct from boot artifacts and guest rootfs configuration.\r\n    Linked goals (2): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-04\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVDfEyGkVf\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-01\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-02\u001b[39m - Port must support one bounded attached-volume workflow through canonical \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mmachine launch\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mstatus\u001b[0m, and \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mstop\u001b[0m surfaces for the current Firecracker standard lane.\r\n    Linked goals (2): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVDfEyGkVf\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-03\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-03\u001b[39m - Port must keep storage backend, persistence mode, host ownership, and route detail explicit across local, hosted, and SSH-managed execution.\r\n    Linked goals (2): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (2): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVDfEyGkVf\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-02\u001b[39m, \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVDfEyGkVf\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-04\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-04\u001b[39m - Port must publish a proof-backed operator workflow for the first attached-volume lane, including at least one human-reviewable artifact path.\r\n    Linked goals (2): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVDfEyGkVf\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-05\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mNFR-01\u001b[39m - Unsupported storage backends, lanes, or host prerequisites must fail fast with explicit machine, host, and volume detail.\r\n    Linked goals (2): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-04\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVDfEyGkVf\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-NFR-01\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mNFR-02\u001b[39m - Machines that do not opt into attached volumes must preserve the current artifact and rootfs lifecycle behavior without silent changes.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-04\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVDfEyGkVf\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-NFR-02\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mNFR-03\u001b[39m - Verification for the first storage slice must use recommended repo-local techniques, including Rust tests, command proofs, and at least one recording-backed human proof path.\r\n    Linked goals (2): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVDfEyGkVf\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-NFR-03\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mPress Release\u001b[0m\r\n  Status:     \u001b[2mnot authored\u001b[0m\r\n  Guidance:   optional; use for large user-facing value shifts\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mProgress\u001b[0m\r\n  Voyages:              1/1 \u001b[32m\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u001b[39m \u001b[32m1/1\u001b[39m\r\n  Stories:              4/4 \u001b[32m\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u001b[39m \u001b[32m4/4\u001b[39m\r\n  ETA:                  complete\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mVerification Strategy\u001b[0m\r\n  Techniques:\r\n    - Prove shared-model and runtime behavior through story-level Rust tests mapped\r\n    - Use command proofs and a recording-backed human proof path to demonstrate the\r\n    - Validate non-functional posture with explicit failure-path checks for\r\n    - first attached-volume workflow end to end.\r\n    - to voyage requirements.\r\n    - unsupported backends, missing paths, and unchanged rootfs-only behavior.\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mVerification Readiness\u001b[0m\r\n  Criteria:              automated 18 | manual 0\r\n  Requirement coverage:  automated 8 | manual 0\r\n  Artifact inventory:    text 9 | media 1 | other 1\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mVoyages\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVDfEyGkVf\u001b[39m\u001b[0m - Attached Volume Contract Foundations (\u001b[32mdone\u001b[39m)\r\n"]
